---
description: Use PRs for medium and large changes (dev → main only)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Pull requests

- **Medium or large** changes (multi-file features, security fixes, API/auth behavior, engine changes, breaking changes) must go through a **GitHub pull request** — not direct commits to `main`.
- **Do not** open feature branches for PRs. Commit on **`dev`**, push **`dev`**, and use **one PR: `dev` → `main`** (create it when needed; do not stack per-topic branches unless the user explicitly asks).
- After a release, CI rebases **`dev`** onto **`main`** when the changelog is reset; avoid long-lived divergence on `CHANGELOG.md`.
- PR description must include **Summary**, **Test plan** (commands run), a pointer to **CHANGELOG** `[Unreleased]`, and a **Linear** section linking `PER-*` issues (see **linear-github.mdc**).
- When you **push new commits to `dev`** while a **`dev` → `main`** PR is already open, **refresh that PR**: run `gh pr edit` (or equivalent) so **title and body** match the full diff on `dev` (all commits since `main`, not just the latest commit). Do this on every push that changes PR scope.
- Small one-line fixes may commit to `dev` without a PR only when explicitly requested; when in doubt, open or update the `dev` → `main` PR.

# PR merge loops (CodeRabbit + CI)

Follow **coderabbit-pr-loop.mdc** for the full checklist (outside-diff reviews, minor comments, merge authority, and anti-patterns).

Each loop wake on the open **`dev` → `main`** PR:

1. **Triage (complete)** — Unresolved review threads, all pull inline comments, **and** CodeRabbit review summary bodies (`Outside diff range comments`). Inline-only triage is not enough.
2. **Fix + resolve (same pass)** — For each still-valid finding (including **Minor** / **Quick win**): implement or dismiss on `dev`, then **resolve the GitHub thread yourself immediately** — CodeRabbit rarely closes threads and open threads cause infinite loop cycles. Test; **CHANGELOG**; commit; push; **`gh pr edit`** if needed.
3. **Verify resolved** — Before arming the watcher, paginate review threads; every addressed CodeRabbit item must be resolved on GitHub (see **coderabbit-pr-loop.mdc**).
4. **Wait** — After a push you made, use **`./scripts/watch-pr-merge-loop.sh <N> --wait`** (foreground, long `block_until_ms`) or background + `notify_on_output` on `^AGENT_LOOP_WAKE_pr-merge`. Do not exit the turn on a capped manual poll while checks are pending.
5. **Merge** — When merge-ready per **coderabbit-pr-loop.mdc** and the user allowed merge in the loop: **`gh pr merge --merge`** in the same pass. Do not stall after green CI + idle CodeRabbit + zero actionable items.

If checks are already idle when you finish work, run triage → merge immediately. If they are not, the watcher must be running before you end the turn.
